{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"- **Management-fee revenue:** The fund pays its unitary management fee to the platform adviser. The adviser retains its contractually negotiated compensation; the sponsor receives the remaining economics under their agreement—not an industry-standard percentage.\n- **Ordinary operating costs:** The sponsor contractually assumes the covered expenses. Those costs reduce its fee remainder; its profit is the residual after covered costs and agreed charges. The arrangement can therefore expose the sponsor to a shortfall, not merely reduced profit. Expenses expressly excluded from the unitary-fee undertaking remain payable by the fund.\n- **Continuing obligation:** The platform adviser remains responsible to the fund for expenses covered by its advisory agreement. Contracting with the sponsor does not discharge that obligation, including if the sponsor fails to pay.\n\n**Worth knowing:** The sponsor agreement allocates economics between businesses; it does not replace the adviser’s commitment to the fund."}}
